## Security and X9 Standard Notes

This chart is intended to support deployments where:
- Payment payload exchange is protected by JWS signatures.
- Certificate trust is validated according to X9 Financial PKI expectations.
- Key material and integration credentials are injected through secret management practices.

This service exposes an open, unauthenticated API. Access control is intentionally out of scope —
protect it at your edge (API gateway, mTLS, or network policy).

From an operations perspective, pay special attention to:
- Keystore and truststore paths/passwords.
- MongoDB URI and TLS/auth settings.

## Swagger Endpoints Overview

Main API groups exposed by the OpenAPI contract:
- Payment Request lifecycle: `POST /api/v1/payment-request`, `GET/PATCH /api/v1/payment-request/{id}`, `PUT /api/v1/payment-request/{id}/status-update`
- Signature utilities: `POST /api/v1/signature/generate`, `POST /api/v1/signature/validate`
- Public X9 endpoints: `GET /pub/.well-known/jwks`, `GET /pub/.well-known/certificate/{pemFileName}`, `POST /pub/api/v1/loc/{id}`, `POST /pub/api/v1/payment-notification`
- EMV decoding helper endpoint: `POST /api/v1/qrcode-emv-decoder`

Complete API details are available in the project OpenAPI file under Matera Portal.

